BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Translator to Translator: Translating Diaspora
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T190000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261008T210000
DTSTAMP:20261007T060815Z
UID:dothebay-17930016@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Literature
DESCRIPTION:Aaron Coleman and Jon Cho-Polizzi discuss the challenges and r
 evelations of translating the Black diaspora: examining continuities and r
 uptures across languages\, geographies\, and time. The global popularity o
 f Black American culture can provide a reference point across the Black di
 aspora\, but it also serves to obscure local traditions of art and resista
 nce that have developed both independently and in conversation with other 
 diasporic narratives over centuries.\n\nAaron will discuss his own work as
  a poet and its influence on his practice in the context of his 2024 trans
 lation of Afro-Cuban poet Nicolás Guillén's The Great Zoo\, while Jon re
 flects on the growing visibility of Black and Afro-German art and literatu
 re.\n\nAbout Translator to Translator\n\nTranslator to Translator is a tra
 nslator-curated event series at CAT featuring conversations about the inte
 rsections of literature\, activism\, and identity.\n\nThis event series pl
 aces the Center for the Art of Translation’s (CAT’s) public programmin
 g resources directly into the hands of translators\, empowering them to cu
 rate provocative and timely conversations about language\, global literatu
 re\, and the art of translation. By inviting guest curators to shape our p
 rogramming\, we are creating a space for dream interviews\, deep investiga
 tions\, and fresh perspectives on the work we love.\n\nThis series is desi
 gned to strengthen our translator community and bring new voices into the 
 discussion. Whether you are a translator\, an author\, or simp...\n\nFree\
 nKALW Public Media\n\nTickets: https://events.humanitix.com/translator-to-
 translator-translating-diaspora\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026
 /10/8/translator-to-translator-translating-diaspora-tickets\nSource: DoThe
 Bay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34835205/0243728e-314f-4f76-aa85-305508633b81.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261007T060815Z
LOCATION:KALW @ 220 Montgomery\, 220 Montgomery St\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94104
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/8/translator-to-translator-transla
 ting-diaspora-tickets
END:VEVENT
