DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizersKREAMZ.COMWho Goes First? sKr
 eamz’s “Coven” Haunted House Opens October 9 in Fairfield\nEight nig
 hts of Halloween scares will help support Fairfield PAL’s Career Café\n
 \nFAIRFIELD\, Calif. — Everyone has a friend who says they never get sca
 red. This October\, invite them to go first. sKreamz’s Coven Haunted Hou
 se opens October 9 at Solano Town Center for eight nights of Halloween sca
 res.\nProceeds from the event will be donated to Fairfield PAL to support 
 its Career Café program\, which helps local teens explore careers and bui
 ld workplace skills through mentorship\, job shadowing and hands-on learni
 ng.\nCoven runs October 9–10\, 16–17\, 23–24 and 30–31\, from 7:30
  to 10 p.m. The haunted house is located at 1795 Pennsylvania Avenue in Fa
 irfield\, behind JCPenney at Solano Town Center.\nAdmission is $14 per per
 son\, or $12 with a current student\, military or first responder ID.\nAll
  guests must complete a waiver. Guests ages 17 and under need a waiver sig
 ned by a parent or legal guardian\, and children ages 14 and under must at
 tend with a parent or legal guardian.\nChoose a night\, gather your friend
 s and download the required waiver at sKreamz.com before visiting.\nAbout 
 Fairfield PAL\nFairfield PAL provides free recreation and enrichment progr
 ams for teens ages 13–18 from Fairfield\, Suisun City and Travis Air For
 ce Base who are enrolled in middle or high school. Through programs such a
 s Career Café\, PAL helps teens build skills\, strengthen relationships a
 nd prepa...\n\n$12.00\n\nTickets: https://www.skreamz.com/\nDetails: https
 ://sf.funcheap.com/skreamz-coven-haunted-house-fairfield-oct-931/\nSource:
