UID:dothebay-17866469@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:NAZA screens at NEW PEOPLE October 9–11 before moving to The
  Roxie starting October 12.\n\nIn secret conversations on the rooftops of 
 Tel Aviv at night\, the systems behind Israel’s calculated mass killing 
 of Palestinian civilians in Gaza are revealed by the people who designed a
 nd operated them.\n\nDirectors Note:\n\nWe made this film out of a sense o
 f obligation to use our position as Israeli filmmakers and journalists to 
 examine the systems behind the mass killing of Palestinian civilians for w
 hich our country is responsible. While filming members of Israel’s milit
 ary on rooftops at night in Tel Aviv over the past three years\, we found 
 ourselves asking the very questions that were asked by our grandparents’
  generation and throughout the 20th century: how does one group of people 
 allow the total dehumanisation of another?\n\nWhat do the inner workings o
 f such a system look like? Many of the revelations in the film were publis
 hed almost immediately as we learned of them\, in the months following the
  October 7th attacks\, by The Guardian (one of NAZA’s producers)\, in co
 llaboration with reporting partners +972 Magazine and Local Call. The film
  lets us explore something deeper than we could in our investigative journ
 alism alone: not only the words being said but also those that are not sai
 d\, the silence. It is up to all of us to break that silence.\n\n– Yuval
  Abraham and Rachel Szor\n\n“An essential\, devastating documentary…th
 ere’s no turning away from what’s said\, you simply can’t unknow wha
 ...\n\nTickets: https://ticketing.uswest.veezi.com/purchase/22108?siteToke
 n=4m48btf3yavn7xjk5yxk6nc40c\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10
 /12/naza-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7647103;-122.4224081
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34538581/4b9502cc-6b78-43b7-858a-9a9b843b8fe0.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:Roxie Theater\, 3117 16th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94103
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/12/naza-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Profs & Pints San Francisco: The Rise of Vampires
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T180000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261012T210000
DTSTAMP:20261006T172218Z
UID:funcheap-1640929@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lectures Workshops
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerProfs and PintsProfs and Pints
  San Francisco presents: “The Rise of Vampires\,” on the folkloric ori
 gins and literary evolution of today’s fanged fiends\, with Sara Hackenb
 erg\, professor of English at San Francisco State University and scholar o
 f Victorian literature and literature’s vampire tradition.\nDid you know
  that vampires sprang from literature nearly a whole century before Bram S
 toker wrote Dracula\, and that they prowled in folklore for centuries befo
 re that?\n\nYou’d have to visit a lot of gravesites to witness the unear
 thing of as many vampires as will be raised at the October 12th debut of P
 rofs and Pints at The Dairy community space at San Francisco’s Presidio 
 Sports Basement.\nThe excavation will be carried out by Professor Sara Hac
 kenberg\, who previously has given excellent Profs and Pints talks on vamp
 ires and Christmas ghost stories.\nShe’ll show you the vampire beneath t
 he vampire beneath the vampire\, tracing their evolution in old European f
 olklore and the English literature of the nineteenth-century.\nYou’ll ge
 t to know the seductive\, snaky Lamia in Samuel Taylor Coleridge’s 1816 
 poem “Christabel” and the sapphic seductress at the center of Joseph S
 heridan Le Fanu’s 1872 novella Carmilla. You’ll spend time with the ma
 d\, bad\, and dangerous Byronic vampire that originated in John Polidori
 ’s 1819 gothic horror story “The Vampyre\,” found his way into theat
 rical adaptations such as James Planché’s 1820 “The Bride of the Isle
 s\,” and then...\n\n$13.50\n\nTickets: https://events.ticketleap.com/tic
 kets/profsandpints/san-francisco-rise-of-vampires\nDetails: https://sf.fun
 cheap.com/profs-pints-san-francisco-rise-vampires/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/Profs-
 Pints-Circle-Logo.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T172218Z
LOCATION:The Dairy at the Presidio Sports Basement\, 610 Old Mason St\, Sa
 n Francisco\, CA 94129
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/profs-pints-san-francisco-rise-vampires/
END:VEVENT
