BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Mico
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17370141@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:In an era where everyone seemingly wants to blow up overnight\
 , MICO is proof that nothing beats great music and consistency. In late 20
 18\, a 16 year-old Miguel Veloso would sing in Discord servers and Twitch 
 streams to connect with new listeners one-by-one. Now at 21 years old\, MI
 CO’s hard work has paid off in the form of a cult fandom and over 60 mil
 lion global streams all without the aid of a record label.\n\nFor MICO\, t
 he internet isn’t something to be overthought—it’s like his second h
 ome\, organically growing a following of over 750\,000 dedicated “amicos
 ” over the last 5 years. Coming off his radio hit “cut my hair” and 
 sold-out debut show in late 2022\, MICO released his much anticipated EP 
 “the tears we fight” the following September. Followed up by a 3-track
  EP titled “the afterparty” in December\, the sister projects were gen
 erating viral hits like “another soul” and “better”\, with fans co
 ming back for every release.\n\nIn 2023\, MICO sought to break the stigma 
 surrounding online artists by embarking on two tours spanning Canada & the
  US. Selling out a multitude of shows across both countries\, MICO continu
 es to prove the industry wrong\, forcefully becoming one of the main up-an
 d-coming alternative pop artists to breakthrough in recent years.\n\nAnd 2
 024 is showing no signs of stopping for the alt-pop rising phenom\, kickin
 g off the year with his largest show to date at Budweiser Stage in Toronto
 \, and gearing up for a new music era - slated for the Fall - with plans o
 f touring g...\n\nGoldenvoice Presents\n\nTickets: https://tix.axs.com/BTg
 4EgAAAAADWLvAAgAAAAD0%2fv%2f%2f%2fwD%2f%2f%2f%2f%2fC0dvbGRlbnZvaWNlAP%2f%2
 f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f?cid=usaffdostuff\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/
 events/2026/10/13/mico-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7879104;-122.4215079
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/32175807/99d994af-510e-4d92-87fa-7b3a49e1f722.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:The Regency Ballroom\, 1290 Sutter Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94109
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/13/mico-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Zolita
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261013T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T062917Z
UID:dothebay-17499315@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Zolita\nTuesday\, October 13 | ​Rickshaw Stop\n\nZolita has 
 always viewed her songwriting through the lens of a camera\, envisioning h
 ow each lyric and note might play out on screen. While beginning her caree
 r in music\, the multi-hyphenate artist was sharpening her filmmaking skil
 ls at NYU’s Tisch School of the Arts. Marrying these two artistic medium
 s into vibrant\, narrative-driven music videos\, Zolita’s unique approac
 h to storytelling has earned her hundreds of millions of streams\, a sold-
 out headline tour and a fanbase captivated by the rich characters she brin
 gs to life. From the debut of her first song and viral video\, to the brea
 kout success of her “Somebody I F*cked Once” Trilogy in 2022 and now t
 o her upcoming project\, Queen of Hearts\, her passionate and unapologetic
  approach to visual storytelling is at the core of her artistic identity.\
 n\nZolita’s forthcoming sophomore album\, Queen of Hearts\, is built aro
 und a pair of equally ambitious themes. The first offers a bold celebratio
 n of queer love\, joy and acceptance— an invitation for her fans to embr
 ace their individuality and live authentically. The other offers a more pe
 rsonal\, introspective meditation on her past relationships. “I feel lik
 e I got to explore things that I had never written about before—things t
 hat maybe I was a little bit afraid to write about\,” she says. This vul
 nerability and honesty in her songwriting is a moment that the artist born
  Zoë Hoetzel has been building toward for a long time.\nThe project’s f
 i...\n\n$26\, All Ages\nAnother Planet Entertainment Presents: The Hell’
 s Belles Tour\n\nTickets: https://apeconcerts.com/events/zolita-261013/\nD
 etails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/13/zolita-tickets\nSource: DoT
 heBay
GEO:37.7760033;-122.4204681
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/32800634/17c8e2a3-aeb7-4927-ba0b-c6bee6259e74.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T062917Z
LOCATION:Rickshaw Stop\, 155 Fell Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94102
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/13/zolita-tickets
END:VEVENT
