SUMMARY:United Nations Association Film Festival | Opening Night
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T173000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T172218Z
UID:caldiscovery-festival-02f5534465824a5f@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:festival,film
DESCRIPTION:Category: Festivals / ParadesContact Phone: (650) 724-5544Cont
 act Email: info@unaff.orgLink: https://www.unaff.org/The 29th United Natio
 ns Association Film Festival opens Thursday\, Oct. 15\, at Mitchell Park C
 ommunity Center in Palo Alto\, with remarks by Mayor Vickie Veenker and th
 e presentation of a City of Palo Alto proclamation recognizing the 29th UN
 AFF.Opening Night begins with the West Coast premiere of The Comfort Dogs 
 of Uganda\, directed by Australian filmmaker Richard Wainwright. The docum
 entary follows former child soldiers in northern Uganda finding unexpected
  bonds with rescued village dogs.Next is the world premiere of Last Christ
 ian in Bethlehem\, from local Bay Area team and UNAFF alums\, Robert Lever
 ing\, Stephen Talbot\, and Stephanie Mechura. This feature documentary pro
 vides interviews and footage of Palestinian Christians living in the West 
 Bank. The night concludes with Through the Body\, a film about Keith Terry
 \, an Oakland percussionist and dancer. Director Andrew Reissiger journeys
  with Terry as he builds a global community through the International Body
  Music Festival. A special dance performance will also take place at this 
 screening.\n\nPublished by KGO\nContains information from CalDiscovery (ca
 ldiscovery.com)\, ODbL 1.0\n\nDetails: https://www.unaff.org/?utm_source=c
 aldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-francisco-ca\nSource: CalDisco
 very
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T172218Z
LOCATION:Mitchell Park Community Center 3700 Middlefield Road Palo Alto
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.unaff.org/?utm_source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_camp
 aign=san-francisco-ca
END:VEVENT
