SUMMARY:The Blasting Company
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001200Z
UID:dothebay-17524330@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:It’s not very well-worn\, but the Nashville street band to c
 omposer pipeline has certainly been a distinctive\, if tempered\, fairy-ta
 le arc for Joshua Kaufman and Justin Rubenstein\, the brothers at the helm
  of The Blasting Company. For years\, curiosity and circumstance guided th
 em through the streets of the US and Europe as they accumulated a blend of
  American folk and Eastern European influences\, grand orchestral tendenci
 es\, and inescapably modern sensibilities\, eventually landing them in Los
  Angeles\, where they found a home for most of it in the world of film and
  television. Their first and perhaps most notable venture into scoring was
  for the critically-acclaimed animated miniseries\, Over the Garden Wall\,
  which has become a seasonal staple for a growing fanbase worldwide whenev
 er fall - or its equatorial approximate - is in the air. Other composing v
 entures include music written for Burlesque\, the New York Times/ Serial p
 odcast The Kids of Rutherford County\, Adult Swim’s The Elephant\, and a
  threealbum soundtrack for table top role playing campaign\, The Crooked M
 oon. Their recent releases feature collaborations with Tom Kenny (Spongebo
 b Squarepants)\, Haley Reinhart (Post-Modern Jukebox)\, Jemaine Clement (F
 light of the Concords)\, and one of their all-time musical heroes\, arrang
 er and composer Van Dyke Parks. The Blasting Company's journey has been on
 e dedicated to their artistic community and their craft. This\, and the ea
 gerness with which they explore music’s expansive storyt...\n\nGoldenvoi
 ce Presents\n\nTickets: https://tix.axs.com/BTg4EgAAAAD39SXFAgAAAAAJ%2fv%2
 f%2f%2fwD%2f%2f%2f%2f%2fC0dvbGRlbnZvaWNlAP%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f%2f?c
 id=usaffdostuff\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/15/the-blast
 ing-company-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7879104;-122.4215079
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/32918907/49ebeae5-5f9d-4038-9b2b-353b7dd2841f.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001200Z
LOCATION:The Regency Ballroom\, 1290 Sutter Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94109
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/15/the-blasting-company-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Bluegrass Tribute To Dr. Ralph Stanley By His Grandson (Berkeley)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261015T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1634349@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Community
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerNathan Stanley’s “Personal
  Tribute to Dr. Ralph Stanley” is a heartfelt celebration of the life\, 
 legacy\, and timeless music of his grandfather\, the legendary bluegrass p
 ioneer Dr. Ralph Stanley. Carrying forward the Stanley family tradition\, 
 Nathan honors the songs\, stories\, and spirit that made Dr. Ralph Stanley
  an icon of American music. With his powerful voice\, deep connection to t
 he music\, and personal memories from a lifetime around his grandfather\, 
 Nathan brings audiences an unforgettable evening filled with authentic blu
 egrass\, emotion\, and Appalachian heritage. A Dove Award winner\, Grammy 
 nominee\, and ICM Award winner\, Nathan Stanley continues the mission of p
 reserving and sharing the music that helped inspire generations. His tribu
 te show celebrates not only the remarkable career of Dr. Ralph Stanley\, b
 ut also the family bond and musical legacy that continues to live on. Don
 ’t miss this heartfelt tribute honoring one of bluegrass music’s great
 est legends\, performed by the grandson who knew him best. Nathan Stanley 
 was the last lead singer for Dr. Ralph Stanley & The Clinch Mountain Boys.
  Tickets are $35 in advance\, $40 at the door general admission\; $30 for 
 student/low income individuals. Children under 12 are free. Advance ticket
 s are available here\, or if the show is not sold out\, you may purchase y
 our tickets at the door before the show. Doors open 30 minutes before show
  time. We accept cash or Venmo only at the door.\n\n$35.00\n\nTickets: htt
 ps://www.eventvesta.com/events/160689-a-special-tribute-to-dr-ralph-stanle
 y-starring-nathan-stanley-constant-sorrow\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.co
 m/bluegrass-tribute-dr-ralph-stanley-grandson-berkeley/\nSource: Funcheap 
 SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/image-
 78.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:The Back Room 1984 Bonita Ave\, Berkeley CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/bluegrass-tribute-dr-ralph-stanley-grandson-be
 rkeley/
END:VEVENT
