DESCRIPTION:Filipino American International Book Festival (SF Main Library
 )\nSan Francisco Public Library\nOct. 17-18\, 10 a.m. to 5:30 p.m. both da
 ys\nExplore the richness and variety of Filipino diasporic literature this
  Filipino American History Month. The Filipino American International Book
  Festival (FilBookFest) returns in October for its 8th iteration\, continu
 ing its legacy as the largest Filipino American literary festival in the U
 .S.\nFilBookFest brings together an exciting array of writers\, scholars a
 nd creatives from across the globe\, including the U.S\, Canada and the Ph
 ilippines\, to San Francisco Public Library.\n\nEnjoy panel discussions\, 
 book signings and readings featuring a vibrant mix of established and emer
 ging voices. This two-day event is a celebration of storytelling\, culture
  and the diverse experiences of the Filipino diaspora.\nPresented by San F
 rancisco Public Library\n\nUpcoming Filipino American International Book F
 estival (SF Main Library) Events\nSat 10/17 Filipino American Internationa
 l Book Festival (SF Main Library)Disclaimer: Please double check event inf
 ormation with the event organizer as events can be canceled\, details can 
 change after they are added to our calendar\, and errors do occur.\n\nFree
 \n\nTickets: https://on.sfpl.org/FilBookFest-26\nDetails: https://sf.funch
 eap.com/filipino-american-international-book-festival-sf-main-library/\nSo
 urce: Funcheap SF
