BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:United Nations Association Film Festival | Free UNAFF & Kids Progr
 am
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261017T134500
DTSTAMP:20261006T172218Z
UID:caldiscovery-festival-2551c3f8895e5b14@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:family,festival,film,free
DESCRIPTION:Category: Festivals / ParadesContact Phone: (650) 724-5544Cont
 act Email: info@unaff.orgCost: FreeLink: https://www.unaff.org/The 29th Un
 ited Nations Association Film Festival presents free programming for kids 
 on Saturday\, Oct. 17\, in Palo Alto\, featuring two short documentaries.T
 he program opens with the world premiere of "The Fixer\," a 12-minute stop
 -motion documentary from local filmmakers Mimi Chakarova and Lydia Chávez
 . The film follows a 10-year-old girl determined to fix what is broken in 
 a fragile world.The program continues with "Under the Canopy\," directed b
 y Michal Krawczyk. Set in Colombia’s Andean-Amazon Piedmont\, the docume
 ntary follows a community-led effort to map biodiversity and restore fores
 ts while preserving Indigenous ecological knowledge.**Admission is free.**
  This special UNAFF & Kids Program offers an opportunity to see two short 
 documentaries suitable for all audiences. The 29th UNAFF runs Oct. 15-25\,
  2026\, with the theme “Passion for Change.” The festival features fil
 ms addressing human rights issues\, including the environment\, women’s 
 rights\, racism and peace\, and engages audiences throughout the Bay Area.
 \n\nPublished by KGO\nContains information from CalDiscovery (caldiscovery
 .com)\, ODbL 1.0\n\nDetails: https://www.unaff.org/?utm_source=caldiscover
 y&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-francisco-ca\nSource: CalDiscovery
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T172218Z
LOCATION:Mitchell Park Community Center 3700 Middlefield Road Palo Alto
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.unaff.org/?utm_source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_camp
 aign=san-francisco-ca
END:VEVENT
