 t your lederhosen and dirndl dress! SideTrack's Oktoberfest celebration is
  back\, bringing a biergarten experience to downtown Pleasanton on Friday\
 , October 16 and Saturday\, October 17!The two-day event features a specia
 l menu of German food and drink\, live entertainment by Polkageist West\, 
 fun games and plenty of festive decor! The event is free to attend with fo
 od and drink tickets available for purchase at the door. For guests lookin
 g to guarantee a spot inside the tents each evening\, packages are availab
 le for pre-purchase which include seats\, food and drink and a limited edi
 tion beer stein. Enjoy menu of Oktoberfest-inspired food and drink includi
 ng Za German Plate with sausages\, German potato salad\, red cabbage and s
 auerkraut and Za Vorks - the Za German Plate with a beer in commemorative 
 SideTrack stein (limited quantities). A menu of a la carte items includes 
 pretzels and special items for kids like hot dogs\, mac and cheese and tat
 er tots. SideTrack also welcomes back Pleasanton’s Primrose Bakery\, sel
 ling their German cookies and cakes throughout the weekend while local bre
 weries will be featured alongside traditional German beer like Hofbräu M
 ünchen and Paulaner Oktoberfest Märzen. Wine and additional beverages ar
 e available as well. Tickets + Pricing: Admission is...\n\nPublished by KG
