BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Fall Family Festival
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T000000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T030000
DTSTAMP:20261006T002614Z
UID:caldiscovery-festival-1927cbf549bdf247@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:festival,free
DESCRIPTION:Taking place under the twinkling Spectra lights\, the Fall Fam
 ily Festival on October 17th\, from 4 to 7pm\; features fun carnival games
 \, free pumpkin decorating\, face painting\, the San Francisco Public Libr
 ary Bookmobile\, and entertainment such as stilt walkers and bubble magic 
 with Sterling Bubble.\nThe selfie station with the autumn-themed Petalz Fl
 ower Truck is a must stop photo op with City Hall as the backdrop\, as are
  the carnival treats: cotton candy\, candy apples and local food trucks fe
 aturing fall fair favorites.\nSign up on Eventbrite for an event day remin
 der\, but no ticket needed to attend this free event.\nThis event is spons
 ored by: Avenue Greenlight\, an investment engine for San Francisco’s co
 mmunity projects\, providing high-impact grants with tangible results\; al
 ong with Civic Center Community Benefit District\, Illuminate\, the San Fr
 ancisco Public Library and San Francisco Recreation & Parks Department.\n\
 nAlso be sure to check out adjacent kid & family events\, San Francisco Di
 strict Attorney’s Office‘s Keepin’ It Safe in the City (Civic Center
  Plaza\, 10am-2pm) and Market Street Arts‘ Market Street Arts & Theater 
 Festival (many locations\, including UN Plaza\, with circus and aerial per
 formances in the evening\, event runs 4-10pm).\n\nPublished by SF Civic Ce
 nter\nContains information from CalDiscovery (caldiscovery.com)\, ODbL 1.0
 \n\nDetails: https://sfciviccenter.org/event/fall-family-festival/?utm_sou
