SUMMARY:31st Annual Campbell Oktoberfest
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T180000
DTSTAMP:20261006T160356Z
UID:caldiscovery-festival-bc0e495c119b3d97@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:festival
DESCRIPTION:Category: Festivals / ParadesContact Name: Campbell ChamberCon
 tact Phone: 408-378-6252Contact Email: info@campbellchamber.netCost: Free 
 admissionLink: https://campbelloktoberfest.comWillkommen to Campbell Oktob
 erfest: 31 Years of Bavarian CheerGrab your dirndl\, dust off your lederho
 sen\, and get ready for two full days of Gemütlichkeit in the heart of Do
 wntown Campbell. For 31 years running\, the Campbell Chamber has thrown on
 e of the most authentic Bavarian celebrations in the Bay Area\, and this O
 ctober\, the Prost is on us.Saturday\, October 17th | 10am–6pmSunday\, O
 ctober 18th | 10am–5pmDowntown CampbellBrowse 125+ artisan and business 
 booths\, feast on sweet and savory German fare\, and sip your way through 
 a stellar lineup of wine and beer all set to the soundtrack of some of the
  Bay Area's best live bands across four stages.At the center of it all is 
 the Biersch Garten\, the beating heart of the festival. Beneath the expans
 ive covered tents\, friends and family gather to eat\, drink\, and be merr
 y with plates of hearty German classics and the finest brews from Gordon B
 iersch Brewing Company. The Zicke Zacke Band keeps the oompah going all we
 ekend long\, while bold contestants battle it out in the Stein-Holding Con
 test\, and festival-goers show off their finest Bavarian style in the Best
  Dressed Contest.Biersch Garten Happenings• 🎶 Zicke Zacke Band — 10
 am–6pm Sat / 10am–5pm Sun• 🍻 VIP Area with premier seating and sp
 ecial food & drink• 👗 Best Dressed Contest — 2pm both days• 🍺 
 Stein-...\n\nPublished by KGO\nContains information from CalDiscovery (cal
 discovery.com)\, ODbL 1.0\n\nDetails: https://campbelloktoberfest.com?utm_
 source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_campaign=san-francisco-ca\nSource: 
 CalDiscovery
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T160356Z
LOCATION:Along East Campbell Avenue and side streets in Downtown Campbell 
 CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://campbelloktoberfest.com?utm_source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics
 &utm_campaign=san-francisco-ca
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:“Manny’s Neighborhood Trash Cleanup” w/ $1 Beer & Free Yoga 
 Classes\, Free Fries
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T110000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1633249@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Free Food
DESCRIPTION:“Manny’s Neighborhood Trash Cleanup” w/ $1 Beer & Free Y
 oga Classes\, Free Fries (SF)\nManny's\nTired? Sunday Funday. Wired? Sunda
 y done-day. Make our neighborhood better\, brunch with cool people (sorry 
 not sorry\, we’re biased)\, get deals to some fave local spots\, and wra
 p it up before the Sunday Scaries hit with an easy hour of picking up tras
 h around our neighborhood with friends and the community!\nRSVP to save yo
 ur spot\nSF Public Works\, TogetherSF\, Shine On SF\, and Manny’s is hos
 ting a weekly neighborhood trash pick up to help keep our area clean and n
 eat.\n\nBy picking up with us\, you’ll get a special certificate that in
 cludes a whole host of neighborhood discounts valid that day\, including:\
 n\n$3 well highballs and $1 PBRs – Blondies\nHalf price shots (specific 
 shots only) – Bond Bar\nFree Tasty Small Fries – Beehive Bar\nOne free
  Yoga Class – HAUM Yoga\nOne free Yoga Class – Love Story Yoga\n2 for 
 1 empanadas – Venga Empanadas\nOne drink ticket (beer or wine) – Curio
  Bar\nFree Small Hot Chocolate – Dandelion Chocolate\n2 for 1 draft beer
  – Standard Deviant\nFrozen margarita with any additional purchase – W
 est of Pecos\nPlease note that the discounts might vary!\n\nWe’ll provid
 e the gear. All you need to bring is yourself(and maybe the two or three f
 riends you get to sign up to enjoy those 2-1 empanadas). When we’re done
 \, and before you settle in for those dollar margs\, join us for brunch to
  support Farming Hope – the non-profit restaurant at Manny’s! Don’t 
 forget to bring layers and comfo...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://refuserefu
 sesf.org/cleanups\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/mannys-neighborhood-tr
 ash-cleanup-w-1-beer-free-yoga-classes-free-fries-sf-154/\nSource: Funchea
 p SF
