CATEGORIES:Outdoors
DESCRIPTION:Make a Friend Picnic 2026: BYO Picnic Setup (SF)Make a Friend 
 Picnic is a casual outdoor social meetup at Potrero del Sol Park for peopl
 e looking to meet new people in San Francisco. Attendees are asked to brin
 g their own blanket\, drinks\, snacks\, and other picnic supplies. The hos
 t plans informal activities to make conversations easier\, and Athena the 
 dog will also attend.\nOriginal Event Description:\n_Make a Friend Picnic\
 nA REAL UPDATE: WE HAVE A DATE. 🎉\nMost importantly: you’re all aweso
 me.\nYou signed up to a stranger’s event because you wanted to make a fr
 iend. You put yourself out there to meet people you don’t know\, which i
 s hard\, and you did it anyway.\nSo thank you. That took guts\, and I wasn
 ’t going to let that go to waste.\nWhen I first made this event\, it was
  20 people and a blanket. Then it became 505 of you\, plus a waitlist\, wh
 ich was genuinely insane and also one of the nicest things that’s happen
 ed since I moved here.\nNaturally\, that also created a tiny logistical pr
 oblem: several hundred people showing up to a public park requires a permi
 t.\nSo I went to SF Rec and Park\, explained exactly what happened\, and a
 fter a lot of back and forth\, we officially have a new plan: October 18 a
 t Potrero Park.\nSince this has become much bigger than the original “pe
 ople sitting on blankets making friends” plan\, I’m also putting toget
 her a few fun\, easy activations to help people connect once they get ther
 e. Nothing mandatory or overly structured\, just things that make talking 
 to a...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://partiful.com/e/NnTYzma0yrGAehRuRl1v?so
 urce=discover\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-friend-picnic-bringyou
 rownblanket-potrero-del-sol-park/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/imgi_1
 8_cBloUF-j9F4khU67t38Lk.png
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:Potrero del Sol Park (La Raza)\, Potrero Avenue and 25th Street\,
  San Francisco\, CA
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/sfs-friend-picnic-bringyourownblanket-potrero-
 del-sol-park/
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:United Nations Association Film Festival | Free Shorts Program
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261018T140000
DTSTAMP:20261006T172218Z
UID:caldiscovery-festival-ba0850293f5124ea@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:festival,film,free
DESCRIPTION:Category: Festivals / ParadesContact Phone: (650) 724-5544Cont
 act Email: info@unaff.orgCost: FreeLink: https://www.unaff.org/The 29th Un
 ited Nations Association Film Festival presents a free shorts program on S
 unday\, Oct. 18\, in Palo Alto\, featuring three documentaries that explor
 e wildlife conservation\, wrongful incarceration\, and the global impact o
 f cryptocurrency.The program opens with "Crossing the Divide\," directed a
 nd produced by local filmmaker Talia Frank. The 11-minute documentary exam
 ines how roads fragment wildlife habitats and explores the potential of wi
 ldlife crossings to restore animal movement and strengthen ecosystems.Next
  is "The Dreaming Game\," directed and produced by Jordan Salvatoriello. T
 he film follows 70-year-old Raymond Gaines\, a Boston native and lifelong 
 baseball fan\, as he returns to Fenway Park after spending 47 years in pri
 son for a murder he did not commit. As he awaits a decision on his case\, 
 Gaines works to rebuild his life and pursue his long-sought freedom. The p
 rogram concludes with "The Market and the Monkey’s Paw\," directed and p
 roduced by "Graham New\, Leo Safir\, and Oliver Richards. Set in El Salvad
 or\, the documentary explores the country’s adoption of Bitcoin as legal
  tender through the perspectives of market vendors\, educators and communi
 ty members\, examining questions of economic inclusion\, tourism\, gentrif
 ication and digital finance.**Admission is free.** The special program fro
 m UNAFF offers an opportunity to see three short docum...\n\nPublished by 
 KGO\nContains information from CalDiscovery (caldiscovery.com)\, ODbL 1.0\
 n\nDetails: https://www.unaff.org/?utm_source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&
 utm_campaign=san-francisco-ca\nSource: CalDiscovery
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T172218Z
LOCATION:Mitchell Park Community Center 3700 Middlefield Road Palo Alto
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://www.unaff.org/?utm_source=caldiscovery&utm_medium=ics&utm_camp
 aign=san-francisco-ca
END:VEVENT
