BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:United Nations Association Film Festival | Free UNAFF in Schools P
 rogram
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T151500
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261021T170000
DTSTAMP:20261006T172218Z
UID:caldiscovery-festival-1a37157941e9928a@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:1
CATEGORIES:festival,film,free
DESCRIPTION:Category: Festivals / ParadesContact Phone: (650) 724-5544Cont
 act Email: info@unaff.orgCost: FreeLink: https://www.unaff.org/The 29th Un
 ited Nations Association Film Festival presents UNAFF in Schools\, a free 
 program for students and teachers on Wednesday\, Oct. 21\, in East Palo Al
 to. The program features two documentaries exploring marine conservation\,
  environmental sustainability and community action.The program opens with 
 Constellations of the Sea\, directed and produced by Addie Knoll. The film
  follows marine biologists in the Maldives as they study and track endange
 red whale sharks\, exploring the relationship between conservation\, touri
 sm and the ocean.The program continues with Saving Walden’s World\, dire
 cted and produced by Jim Merkel\, who previously lived in San Luis Obispo.
  The documentary follows Merkel’s decades-long journey from arms dealer 
 to environmental advocate as he raises his son on an off-the-grid homestea
 d and explores approaches to sustainability around the world.**Admission i
 s free for students and teachers.** This special UNAFF in Schools program 
 offers an opportunity for students and teachers to see two documentaries. 
 The 29th UNAFF runs Oct. 15-25\, 2026\, with the theme “Passion for Chan
 ge.” The festival features films addressing human rights issues\, includ
 ing the environment\, women’s rights\, racism and peace\, and engages au
