BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:DIY Taxidermy Rat Workshop
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T080000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T100000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17672037@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:Calling someone a "rat" is generally seen as a bad thing—but
  is it really? As the owner of several rats (yes\, the guy writing this co
 py)\, I can tell you firsthand that rats are amazing\, cute\, and very cle
 an animals. Sure\, they get hit with the whole “Well\, the Black Plague 
 was their fault” thing\, but we all know it was really the fleas. No exp
 erience? No problem. This class is perfect for anyone looking to dip their
  toes into the world of taxidermy. We’ll walk (scurry?) you through ever
 y step. You’ll leave with a newfound skill\, a tiny new friend\, and pro
 bably a weird story to tell at parties.\n\nThe instructor\, Mr. Vassallo h
 as over thirty-five years experience as a professional taxidermist and tea
 cher. He has traveled Continental North America\, Alaska\, Hawaii\, Mexico
 \, Europe and Africa studying\, collecting and preserving wildlife.\n\nImp
 ortant Details:\nClasses will be held at 766 Valencia St.\, San Francisco\
 nPre-registration required as materials must be prepared for each student 
 and space is VERY limited.\nChildren under 18 must be accompanied by an ad
 ult. We ask that all attendees be over the age of 14. Special exceptions m
 ay be made by contacting us before you purchase your spot.\nStudents are e
 ncouraged to bring lunch/snacks.\nPlease arrive promptly at the start time
 .\nCancellations must be made at least 72 hours prior to the date of the c
 lass. Cancellations will then be converted to credit that can either be us
 ed toward merchandise in the store or to enroll in another workshop....\n\
 n$225\, 18+ or with Guardian\nPaxton Gate's\n\nTickets: https://paxtongate
 .com/products/taxidermy-rat-class\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/20
 26/10/31/diy-taxidermy-rat-workshop-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7596242;-122.4217046
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33616885/aeb7c48d-458a-4431-ab09-96b26d3dfa1c.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Paxton Gate\, 824 Valencia Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/10/31/diy-taxidermy-rat-workshop-tick
 ets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Free “Legion of Honor” Museum Day for Bay Area Residents (Ever
 y Saturday)
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T093000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261031T171500
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1639367@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Art Museums
DESCRIPTION:Free “Legion of Honor” Museum Day for Bay Area Residents (
 Every Saturday)\n© StephanHoerold Getty Images Signature via Canva.com\nE
 very Saturday the Legion of Honor offers free general admission to the per
 manent galleries to Bay Area residents. Advanced tickets are required\, an
 d capacity is limited due to COVID-19 precautions.\nPlease note that admis
 sion to any special exhibits is not included nor discounted and will requi
 re the full admission price.\nSaturdays feature engaging art experiences f
 or the entire family\, including art-making\, gallery guides\, and tours w
 ith discussion and sketching in the permanent galleries.\n\nFree Saturdays
  for Bay Area Residents\nLegion of Honor\nLincoln Park \\ 100 34th Avenue\
 , San Francisco\, CA 94121\n– Most Saturdays\n– Hours are typically 9:
 30 am–5:15 pm\nReserve tickets in advance to skip the line\n\nThis offer
  applies only to general admission for the permanent collection galleries.
 \nFull-priced admission to special exhibitions still applies.\nFor: Reside
 nts of Alameda\, Contra Costa\, Marin\, Napa\, San Francisco\, San Mateo\,
  Santa Clara\, Solano\, and Sonoma Counties with valid photo ID or postmar
 ked envelope bearing home address\nDates and times: Every Saturday beginni
 ng October 19\, 9:30 am–5:15 pm\n\nVisitors ages 17 and under always rec
 eive free admission to the permanent collection galleries.\nPlease note th
 is free Saturdays offer could be changed or canceled at anytime. Visit leg
 ionofhonor.famsf.org for updates before attending.\nEssential and Frontlin
