SUMMARY:Lucy Bedroque
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17752476@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Music
DESCRIPTION:Los Angeles based nineteen year old Jeremiah Mark (they/he) re
 leased their first full-length endeavor under the moniker Lucy Bedroque\, 
 their deadAir Records debut. With no prior singles\, the breakneck sevente
 en track shotgun blast of Digicore and Hardcore Hip Hop\, titled “Unmusi
 que” has established them as a bastion of these underground sounds. The 
 release date coincided with their first show on the Jane Remover and Dazeg
 xd tour “TURN UP OR DIE”\, along with a full west coast run. Leading u
 p to this moment\, Lucy Bedroque gained a cult following in the shadowy se
 ctors of the online underground\, with a break-out debut LP “Sisterhood
 ” as Lostrushi. This is the name that raised them to notoriety alongside
  peers 9lives\, prettifun\, and egobreak. The new material continues furth
 er down the same path\, combining cutthroat rage\, with the eclecticism an
 d sensitivities of Stereolab\, Radiohead\, and Deftones. While forging the
 ir distinct multi-media surrealism\, Mark also found a penchant for custom
 ized linguistics and contorting the English language. Most notably\, the t
 itle “Glutmother” (the name fans chose for a hyper-active Subreddit) g
 races the cover art of the debut and the packaging of “Unmusique. “The
  role of motherhood here is representative of a superiority to everything 
 around it. But beyond humans\, it’s a reference to mother nature and cre
 ation.” They explain. As for why it’s juxtaposed with gluttony\, that
 ’s because “People want more than anyone can handle\, and I’ve respo
 nded to i...\n\nGoldenvoice Presents\n\nTickets: https://shop.axs.com/?c=a
 xs&e=30567424546772061\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/6/luc
 y-bedroque-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7879104;-122.4215079
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34000418/4d278108-125f-40df-b085-30020f8c2238.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:The Regency Ballroom\, 1290 Sutter Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 
 94109
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/6/lucy-bedroque-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Robert Shields: My Life as a Robot
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T200000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261106T220000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17882159@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Film
DESCRIPTION:Robert Shields: My Life as a Robot celebrates the extraordinar
 y\, and often invisible\, impact one artist can have on the world. In the 
 1970s\, Robert Shields began performing his signature robot routine outsid
 e the Hollywood Wax Museum before later moving to street performances in S
 an Francisco’s Union Square. Within a few short years\, he and his wife\
 , Lorene Yarnell\, were headlining their own hit CBS variety series\, The 
 Shields & Yarnell Show. What Robert didn’t fully realize at the time was
  that his robot would go on to influence the DNA of popping\, locking\, an
 d hip-hop dance as we know it today.\n\nFunny\, joyful\, and full of genui
 ne wonder\, the film introduces you to a man who makes you believe anythin
 g is possible — including\, as Robert demonstrates\, street skiing throu
 gh downtown San Francisco.\n\nFollowed by a live performance by Poppin Joh
 n\; a Q&A with Robert Shields\, director Mark Bonn\, producer Christine Se
 ibert Bonn\, and Poppin John\, moderated by Peter L. Stein\; and a post-sc
 reening reception in the lobby.\n\nInfo and tickets: https://sfdancefilmfe
 st.org/fall-festival-2026/robert-shields/\n\n$25-45\n2026 SF Dance Film Fe
 stival:\n\nTickets: https://sfdancefilmfest.org/fall-festival-2026/robert-
 shields/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/6/robert-shields-my
 -life-as-a-robot-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
GEO:37.7526148;-122.4078356
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34611227/dbcb1877-9a98-4fac-9345-63e6a7eeccf7.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Brava Theater\, 2781 24th Street\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94110
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/6/robert-shields-my-life-as-a-robo
 t-tickets
END:VEVENT
