BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ann M. Evans and Georgeanne Brennan\, Market Memories Cookbook
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T110000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T130000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17747609@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Shopping
DESCRIPTION:Saturday\, November 21\, 2026\, 11:00 am - 11:45 am\n\nStop by
  the Foodwise Classroom for a cooking demo featuring the seasonal bounty o
 f the Ferry Plaza Farmers Market.\n\nGeorgeanne Brennan is a James Beard a
 nd Julia Child award-winning cookbook author. Her association with farmers
  markets goes back to the 1980s\, when her pioneering seed company\, Le Ma
 rche Seeds\, supplied emerging market growers across the country. Her memo
 ir\, A Pig in Provence\, chronicles her adventures in France\, where she s
 till has a home\, raising pigs and making goats milk cheese. She lives in 
 Winters\, California\, with her husband.\n\nAnn M. Evans is a co-founder o
 f the Davis Farmers Market and the Davis Food Co-op\, and she is a former 
 mayor of Davis\, California. A leading proponent of the Farm-to-School mov
 ement in California\, she worked extensively with former California School
  Superintendent Delaine Eastin and with Alice Waters on multiple projects.
  She writes a weekly column for the Davis Enterprise. This is her third co
 okbook. She lives with her husband in Davis.\n\nThey are the co-authors of
  Market Memories Cookbook: Celebrating 50 Years.\n\nAll demos take place i
 n the Foodwise Classroom (green tent in front of the Ferry Building) and a
 re free to the public\, with recipes and samples for all.\n\nThe demo will
  be followed by a book signing with book sales courtesy of Book Passage.\n
 \nTickets: https://foodwise.org/events/ann-m-evans-and-georgeanne-brennan-
 market-memories-cookbook/\nDetails: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21
 /ann-m-evans-and-georgeanne-brennan-market-memories-cookbook-tickets\nSour
 ce: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/33977363/48350a51-16dc-487a-9f0b-869b109a7584.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Ferry Plaza
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/ann-m-evans-and-georgeanne-bren
 nan-market-memories-cookbook-tickets
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:International Bottled Water Tasting Class
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T113000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261121T133000
DTSTAMP:20261006T003107Z
UID:dothebay-17817859@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Lecture/Education
DESCRIPTION:Think you can tell Fiji from Evian in a blind tasting? Know yo
 ur Topo from your Pellegrino just from looking at the bubbles? Have you ev
 er tried salty sparkling Spanish Vichy Catalan\, or experienced the bizarr
 e Borjomi from the Republic of Georgia?\n\nBottled waters differ dramatica
 lly in texture\, minerality\, carbonation\, and finish. We’ll try lots o
 f waters - some familiar and some super weird- and we’ll learn Why they 
 taste the way they do in this alcohol-free experience.\n\nWe’ll start by
  blind tasting San Francisco tap to see if Hetch Hetchy is as heavenly as 
 we’ve heard about. We’ll continue blind tasting bottled still waters f
 rom neutral to mineral-rich\, then crack open a whole bunch of sparkling s
 oda waters and go through them one-by-one.\n\n$55\n\nTickets: https://clas
 sbento.com/international-bottled-water-tasting-class-san-francisco\nDetail
 s: https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/international-bottled-water-tast
 ing-class-tickets\nSource: DoTheBay
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://assets0.dostuffmedia.com/uploads/aws_asset/aws_ass
 et/34305806/f27c88f8-a0c9-43fd-8cdc-57fcfc10dc27.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T003107Z
LOCATION:Alcademics\, 57 Post Street\, Suite 608\, San Francisco\, CA\, 94
 104
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://dothebay.com/events/2026/11/21/international-bottled-water-tas
 ting-class-tickets
END:VEVENT
