DESCRIPTION:San Francisco Department of Children\, Youth & Their Families 
 (DCYF)\n\nThis is Your City. This is Your Voice. This is Your Future. Shar
 e your story about growing up and raising your family in San Francisco.\n\
 nEvery family has a story. Every voice matters. Please share yours.\nJoin 
 us for the District 3 Chinatown Family Summit! The This Is Your City: Fami
 ly Summit Series invites families\, caregivers\, young people\, and commun
 ity members from across San Francisco to help shape the future of our city
 .\n\nSaturday\, Dec. 12\, 2026\, 11:00 a.m. – 1:30 p.m.\nBetty Ann Ong R
 ecreation Center\, 1199 Mason St\, SF\, CA 94108\n\nFree food\, childcare\
 , and interpretation are provided. Please note all interpretation requests
  must be made 48 hours or more prior to the Family Summit.\nWho should att
 end? Everyone is welcome. This event highlights District 3\, but you can a
 ttend any Family Summit that fits your schedule.\nWhy are we gathering? Th
 e Family Summit Series is part of San Francisco’s first Citywide Communi
 ty Needs Assessment. Through conversations with families across the city\,
  we’re learning what matters most to children\, youth\, young adults\, a
 nd families. What we learn will help improve future planning\, programs\, 
 and services.\nWhether you’ve lived in San Francisco your whole life or 
 recently made it your home\, your experiences and ideas matter.\nDistrict 
 3 Neighborhoods include: Barbary Coast & Northern Waterfront\, Chinatown\,
  Lower Nob Hill\, Financial District\, Fisherman’s Wharf\, Jackson Squar
 e\, Nob...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/district-3-chi
 natown-family-summit-tickets-1996551616631?aff=oddtdtcreator\nDetails: htt
 ps://sf.funcheap.com/district-3-chinatown-family-summit/\nSource: Funcheap
  SF
